# Keep the build context small and hermetic. node_modules in particular must
# never be copied in: the image runs `npm ci` itself, and a host tree built for
# a different libc would poison better-sqlite3 and sharp.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
.git
corpus
docs
.scratch
.impeccable
*.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
infrastructure/.env

# Runtime state. All three are VOLUMES at runtime, and the host copies are
# large, stale and irrelevant to a build.
#
# `data/sources.json` is the exception and is force-included: it is the seed
# list a fresh database is populated from, it is committed, and it is read from
# `/app/data/sources.json` INSIDE the image rather than from the volume. See
# the Dockerfile's note on why the database moved to /data and this file did not.
data/*
!data/sources.json
output
uploads

*.log
**/*.map
coverage
